meta {
  name: Toggle featured status
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/gallery/{{articleId}}/featured
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  # Toggle featured status

  `PATCH /api/gallery/{{articleId}}/featured`

  Invert isFeatured; featuring removes featured status from other articles.

  ## Authentication

  Admin or Editor; inherited Bearer token.

  ## Parameters

  | Name | Location | Meaning |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | articleId | Path | GUID; replace the example with a real resource. |

  ## Request body

  No request body.

  ## Response

  HTTP **200**.

  ```json
  {
    "message": "Article marked as featured.",
    "id": "44444444-4444-4444-8444-444444444444",
    "isFeatured": true
  }
  ```

  ## Errors

  - 404: Gallery article not found.
  - 401: missing, invalid, or expired Bearer token.
  - 403: authenticated token with an insufficient role.

  Automatic model validation can return ValidationProblemDetails; explicit controller errors use a message field. Authentication middleware errors may have no body.

  ## Notes

  No body. Repeating the call reverses the state. Unfeaturing returns message Article unfeatured. and isFeatured=false. Updates updatedAt.

  Examples contain fictitious data. The assertion checks the successful scenario; a missing record or insufficient permissions can produce a different documented status.
}
